# resize: the terminal resized under merl. At 80x24 the long lines of the notes wrap; at 160x48
# they fit, the tree, the code and the status line in place and the cursor still on its line; t
# hides the tree and the widest line fits on one row, t again brings the tree back beside it.
size 80x24
merl docs/notes.md
wait # Release notes for the support team
key :
type 7
key Enter
wait docs/notes.md  7:1
size 160x48
wait 6 - Заказы старше года архивируются, их нельзя вернуть через API: пишите в поддержку платёжного провайдера.
key t
wait 5 - ⚠️ A refund past the 30-day window needs a manager's approval: open the order, press Refund and write the reason in the note, the payment team reads it.
key t
wait │     the payment team reads it.
# #412: scrolled beside the tree into the second row of a wrapped line, t widens the pane and that
# line fits on one row: the cursor stays on line 16, and a letter typed there lands on it.
size 160x13
key Down*9
wait docs/notes.md  16:1
key t Enter
type X
key Escape
wait 16▎X- A cancelled order keeps its total.
# #458: at 80 columns `?` wraps an action too long for its row under its own column, where it was
# cut at the border.
size 80x24
key ?
wait Go to definition of the word under the
